From e4f8a927ab3b15918fb71fc0ba59800b5fb68d50 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mnavahan3 <mnavahan3@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 12:00:22 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] model : add Kimi-K3.1 (DSA lightning indexer on kimi-k3)

Kimi-K3.1-Pro is Kimi-K3 plus a DeepSeek-V3.2-style lightning indexer
on every full-attention (MLA) layer; every other tensor keeps K3's name,
dtype and shape. The indexer is nope-only:

  q = wq_b_idx(q_a_norm(q_a(x)))   k = LayerNorm(wk_idx(x))
  w = weights_proj(x) / sqrt(head_dim * n_head)
  score[kv,t] = sum_h relu(q[h,t] . k[kv]) * w[h,t]  -> top-k cells per query

convert:
- route KimiK31ForConditionalGeneration to the kimi-k3 converter (its
  text_config says KimiLinearForCausalLM, the old 48B architecture)
- handle dsa_config whatever the architecture label, write the indexer
  keys and tensors; fail on unsupported variants (indexer rope, index
  sharing, rmsnorm k_norm, DSA layers != full-attention layers)
- KIMI_K31_DENSE=1 drops the indexer: a plain kimi-k3 GGUF, dense
  attention, exact up to index_topk tokens

llama:
- kimi-k3 reads the optional indexer keys; with them, the MLA layers get
  the indexer tensors and llama_memory_hybrid_idx (indexer key cache cell
  for cell with the MLA cache), and attend to the top-k cells only
- fused lightning indexer and top-k mask when available, plain ops else;
  the mask is cast to f16 for the fused indexer without flash attention
- indexer LayerNorm uses rms_norm_eps, as in vLLM (f_norm_eps was unset)

quantize (kimi-k3):
- keep the indexer tensors (~180M params) unquantized
- keep attn_k_b/attn_v_b unquantized: their 128-wide rows fall back to
  q4_0 and the CPU repack buffer cannot run a 3D q4_0 k_b against the
  permuted query (GGML_ASSERT in ggml_backend_sched_split_graph)

Tested on tiny-random/kimi-k3.1-pro against a CPU PyTorch reference
(Moonshot's K3 modeling + the indexer per vLLM's K3.1 code): last-token
logits NMSE 1e-5 at top-2048 and 5e-5 at top-4 (vs 1.5e-1 for dense,
so the selection is exercised), flash attention on/off, ubatch 512 and 7;
indexer scores match to 4e-8 on identical inputs. test-llama-archs passes
for kimi-k3 (indexer path), kimi-linear, glm5-next, deepseek32, qwen4exp.

